# Timesheet context

The daily-timesheet skill reads this file every run. It's your source of truth for
*who's who* and *which client each activity belongs to*. Keep only confirmed facts;
the skill will propose additions when it learns something new — review and merge
those additions rather than letting them accumulate elsewhere.

You can hand-edit this file at any time. The skill never overwrites it without
showing you the diff first.

Keep it lean: only *your* facts belong here — generic heuristics live in the skill
itself, and the skill checks this file against a size budget (default 14,000 bytes,
see SKILL.md Step 11) after every edit and compacts when it's exceeded.

---

## Preferences

Override the skill's defaults here. Omit any line you're happy with as default.

- **Timezone**: `Pacific/Auckland`  <!-- IANA name; affects AW UTC→local conversion -->
- **AFK threshold for a real break**: `1050s` (17.5 min) — shorter AFK folds into work
- **Lunch detection window**: `11:30`–`14:30` local — longest AFK in here is lunch
- **Work-hours window for AW rendering**: `06:00`–`20:00` local
- **Default Harvest task for client work**: `Gen - Development/Configuration`
- **Default Harvest task for internal/admin time**: `Meeting - Standup Meetings`
- **Display name in window titles**: `<YourFirstName>` (used by Edge profile signal — e.g. titles ending `… - <Profile> - <YourFirstName> - Microsoft Edge`)

## AW buckets

(The skill caches these after first discovery so subsequent runs skip the buckets endpoint.)

- Hostname suffix: `<YOUR-MACHINE-NAME>`  <!-- e.g. WS-113359 -->
- Window: `aw-watcher-window_<HOST>`
- AFK: `aw-watcher-afk_<HOST>`
- Web (Firefox): `aw-watcher-web-firefox_<HOST>`
- Web (Edge/Chrome): `aw-watcher-web-chrome_<HOST>`
- VS Code: `aw-watcher-vscode_<HOST>` (optional)

